#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116156} :activity/id #uuid "a4c1d15d-a43d-51de-bc2d-191d98aa4e53" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050676 :topic/id #uuid "5e0ed384-c5d0-57c1-be41-97361492eb5d" :topic/math-academy-id 1586} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116156 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116506 :tutorial/content "Consider the function ![](images/44/44c838deb3fa8e3182fbd9d4a03f964dc2731730559d00328190e9259bf01762.svg) whose graph is shown below. How can we plot the graph of ![](images/12/120fd26f32d53872d244163d5a4d63931d0f881b62f3f5f7a924a9c06255ba1d.svg)\n\n![](images/1a/1a11bef66d0529418dde00e5713ed5e98f53a948c8a60f83fd056fd9e2c18698.png)\n\nWe can use some points on the graph of ![](images/44/44c838deb3fa8e3182fbd9d4a03f964dc2731730559d00328190e9259bf01762.svg) to find the corresponding points on the graphs of ![](images/a1/a142ed820c2bdafb8c1b7969028c7f4533c66fa772a73954c46f6b5eb91a050f.svg)\n\nFor example, let's take the point ![](images/8f/8f231df171077c673ad3f7611cfd99a5fb2753448232eb64a5a160a42a21a122.svg) The fact that it lies on the graph of ![](images/44/44c838deb3fa8e3182fbd9d4a03f964dc2731730559d00328190e9259bf01762.svg) means ![](images/53/5327a1cd77a2b8abb05cd13fa3d2c65cdd0a7ff447afd71e682a0282118e886c.svg) Then, if ![](images/06/068f771676e51ca5f58fb024dd4635c8da494dc49bd43398585945ce0920a425.svg) we have\n![](images/03/033afdad9ff42ad24f2d0f4388e6065adea3608bf49116364b5c13833ded06cf.svg) \n\nThis means the point ![](images/b2/b2f8b859ae7e2b4fe083670dc262b473bd79b7b1ee50a60712ae5bc13bffb954.svg) that lies on ![](images/44/44c838deb3fa8e3182fbd9d4a03f964dc2731730559d00328190e9259bf01762.svg) has a corresponding point ![](images/e2/e2e718c0eb1b8cf9581404873ddc1cc4512141d32e2fb42b70f516257ec31365.svg) that lies on ![](images/a1/a142ed820c2bdafb8c1b7969028c7f4533c66fa772a73954c46f6b5eb91a050f.svg)\n\nSo, for each point on the graph of ![](images/c9/c956e6cbfb2d94fa56a68a3173ec78f60fee33a9066c9c44ca4096d67d7b1cba.svg) there will be a point on the graph of ![](images/b9/b9b8d001be0277e544ff2d040e5b537ad8d7df49d33027a56021f4ba62497de3.svg) with the *same* ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value and *one half* the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value:\n\n![](images/66/66e2a4dfc65fc35cd4b812ea418df3976c6e23cc002babaadd1921745353de6b.svg)\n\nFinally, we can plot the points and draw the graph of ![](images/29/2994084d895116512b0d26509c9108d059fa2e73bbc4ea785e8535fce4a7f75b.svg)\n\n![](images/8c/8ce6a8fd398025bfb9cd535fbc16db06a2a219e0d2451cf6278d81d4ab5c264a.png)\n\nThe graph of ![](images/b9/b9b8d001be0277e544ff2d040e5b537ad8d7df49d33027a56021f4ba62497de3.svg) is the graph of ![](images/44/44c838deb3fa8e3182fbd9d4a03f964dc2731730559d00328190e9259bf01762.svg) **horizontally scaled** by a factor of ![](images/d7/d7cae033e26adc59eeceb95b5807505dd0242e42982f350c36209152864cf261.svg)\n\nEquivalently, we can say that the original graph is **compressed** by a scale factor of ![](images/27/270d33581e0657a10d567c6cfaa529521b34e20a39c9a29550698cbf252fabfa.svg)\n\nIn general, the transformation ![](images/45/45950fa47c3a14fa07312805dd06e2638388335b9781c6ba1c07c76d7a5b108c.svg) scales the graph of ![](images/44/44c838deb3fa8e3182fbd9d4a03f964dc2731730559d00328190e9259bf01762.svg) horizontally by a factor of ![](images/aa/aad37c78cd66cde5ccbba8aa66a6d18afcb0fd5b7de52471203a690e0645e4c5.svg)\n\n- If ![](images/8d/8dc6f7e80ecaac9fa07890ce1881dd51de319597ae8b1dce821aa03c1f3eff06.svg) is greater than ![](images/76/76543f4805f22715457d55feb2a3c87d0d873bdcb9c1eed7a4f68539269dcf59.svg) the graph is compressed (or squished) towards the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis by a scale factor of ![](images/c7/c7432bf7a520e569e53fdd1a7303ce6b9f940d99e68b5e7ea3196c51acfe2b69.svg)\n\n- If ![](images/8d/8dc6f7e80ecaac9fa07890ce1881dd51de319597ae8b1dce821aa03c1f3eff06.svg) is between ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) and ![](images/76/76543f4805f22715457d55feb2a3c87d0d873bdcb9c1eed7a4f68539269dcf59.svg) the graph is stretched away from the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis by a scale factor of ![](images/c7/c7432bf7a520e569e53fdd1a7303ce6b9f940d99e68b5e7ea3196c51acfe2b69.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "0f9522aa-685f-5492-a439-69c534d5bbef" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3285 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "c0285e1d-13e9-58ab-bba4-cfc15f23ca69" :step/math-academy-id 18031 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116158}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116157 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115264 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115093 :question/id #uuid "57ece1a0-70e5-523f-8f6d-73a2fef43492" :question/math-academy-id "e-4983"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd783d1a-745d-5cd7-a5c3-9a109b6d1350" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115517} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115520} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530509}] :knowledge-point/title "Plotting the Graph of a Horizontally Stretched Function"} :step/id #uuid "f833b0bd-73c5-5268-9213-0c6017d44609" :step/math-academy-id 18032 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116159}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116158 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115265 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115094 :question/id #uuid "9da96071-1bed-5e17-9d59-45948a0aaa5f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4984"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d199ed2c-8188-5d80-9bb6-7b69ae684747" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048838}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115522} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115523} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530501} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530516}] :knowledge-point/title "Plotting the Graph of a Horizontally Compressed Function"} :step/id #uuid "e73f01